{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Pyridoxal phosphate + H2O <=> Pyridoxal + Orthophosphate","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00018","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00018 + C00001 <=> C00250 + C00009","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00114","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"This is the active form of vitamin B 6 serving as a coenzyme for synthesis of amino acids, neurotransmitters (serotonin, norepinephrine), sphingolipids, aminolevulinic acid.  During transamination of amino acids, pyridoxal phosphate is transiently converted into pyridoxamine phosphate (pyridoxamine). [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
