{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"UDP-D-galactose + 2 NAD+ + H2O <=> UDP-D-galacturonate + 2 NADH + 2 H+","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00004","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00052 + 2 C00003 + C00001 <=> C00617 + 2 C00004 + 2 C00080","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00157","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"NADH is the reduced form of NAD+, and NAD+ is the oxidized form of NADH, A coenzyme composed of ribosylnicotinamide 5'-diphosphate coupled to adenosine 5'-phosphate by pyrophosphate linkage. It is found widely in nature and is involved in numerous enzymatic reactions in which it serves as an electron carrier by being alternately oxidized (NAD+) and reduced (NADH). It forms NADP with the addition of a phosphate group to the 2' position of the adenosyl nucleotide through an ester linkage.(Dorland, 27th ed)","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"UDP-D-galactose + 2 NAD+ + H2O <=> UDP-D-galacturonate + 2 NADH + 2 H+","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00052","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00052 + 2 C00003 + C00001 <=> C00617 + 2 C00004 + 2 C00080","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB03501","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"A nucleoside diphosphate sugar which can be epimerized into UDPglucose for entry into the mainstream of carbohydrate metabolism. Serves as a source of galactose in the synthesis of lipopolysaccharides, cerebrosides, and lactose. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"UDP-D-galactose + 2 NAD+ + H2O <=> UDP-D-galacturonate + 2 NADH + 2 H+","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00473","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00052 + 2 C00003 + C00001 <=> C00617 + 2 C00004 + 2 C00080","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00162","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"Retinol and derivatives of retinol that play an essential role in metabolic functioning of the retina, the growth of and differentiation of epithelial tissue, the growth of bone, reproduction, and the immune response. Dietary vitamin A is derived from a variety of carotenoids found in plants. It is enriched in the liver, egg yolks, and the fat component of dairy products. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"UTP + alpha-D-Galactose 1-phosphate <=> Diphosphate + UDP-D-galactose","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00075","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00075 + C00446 <=> C00013 + C00052","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB04005","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"Uridine 5&#39;-(tetrahydrogen triphosphate). A uracil nucleotide containing three phosphate groups esterified to the sugar moiety. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
