{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"L-Citrulline + H2O <=> L-Ornithine + CO2 + NH3","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00327","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00327 + C00001 <=> C00077 + C00011 + C00014","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00155","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"Citrulline is an amino acid.  It is made from ornithine and carbamoyl phosphate in one of the central reactions in the urea cycle. It is also produced from arginine as a by-product of the reaction catalyzed by NOS family.  Its name is derived from citrullus, the Latin word for watermelon, from which it was first isolated.","type":"literal"}},
