{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"L-Tryptophan + H2O <=> Indole + Pyruvate + NH3","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00078","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00078 + C00001 <=> C00463 + C00022 + C00014","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00150","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"An essential amino acid that is necessary for normal growth in infants and for nitrogen balance in adults. It is a precursor of indole alkaloids in plants. It is a precursor of serotonin (hence its use as an antidepressant and sleep aid). It can be a precursor to niacin, albeit inefficiently, in mammals. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"L-Serine + Indole <=> L-Tryptophan + H2O","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00065","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00065 + C00463 <=> C00078 + C00001","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00133","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"A non-essential amino acid occurring in natural form as the L-isomer. It is synthesized from glycine or threonine. It is involved in the biosynthesis of purines; pyrimidines; and other amino acids. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
