{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"2 trans,trans-Farnesyl diphosphate <=> Diphosphate + Presqualene diphosphate","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00004","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"2 C00448 <=> C00013 + C03428","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00157","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"NADH is the reduced form of NAD+, and NAD+ is the oxidized form of NADH, A coenzyme composed of ribosylnicotinamide 5'-diphosphate coupled to adenosine 5'-phosphate by pyrophosphate linkage. It is found widely in nature and is involved in numerous enzymatic reactions in which it serves as an electron carrier by being alternately oxidized (NAD+) and reduced (NADH). It forms NADP with the addition of a phosphate group to the 2' position of the adenosyl nucleotide through an ester linkage.(Dorland, 27th ed)","type":"literal"}},
