{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"ITP + Succinate + CoA <=> IDP + Orthophosphate + Succinyl-CoA","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00042","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00081 + C00042 + C00010 <=> C00104 + C00009 + C00091","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00139","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"A water-soluble, colorless crystal with an acid taste that is used as a chemical intermediate, in medicine, the manufacture of lacquers, and to make perfume esters. It is also used in foods as a sequestrant, buffer, and a neutralizing agent. (Hawley&#39;s Condensed Chemical Dictionary, 12th ed, p1099; McGraw-Hill Dictionary of Scientific and Technical Terms, 4th ed, p1851)","type":"literal"}},
