{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Ethanolamine <=> Acetaldehyde + NH3","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00189","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00189 <=> C00084 + C00014","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB03994","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"A viscous, hygroscopic amino alcohol with an ammoniacal odor. It is widely distributed in biological tissue and is a component of lecithin. It is used as a surfactant, fluorimetric reagent, and to remove CO2 and H2S from natural gas and other gases. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"L-Threonine <=> Glycine + Acetaldehyde","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00188","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00188 <=> C00037 + C00084","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00156","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"An essential amino acid occurring naturally in the L-form, which is the active form. It is found in eggs, milk, gelatin, and other proteins. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
