{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"D-Glucose 6-phosphate <=> D-Fructose 6-phosphate","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00092","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00092 <=> C00085","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB03581","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"An ester of glucose with phosphoric acid, made in the course of glucose metabolism by mammalian and other cells. It is a normal constituent of resting muscle and probably is in constant equilibrium with fructose-6-phosphate. (Stedman, 26th ed)","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"ATP + Urea + HCO3- <=> ADP + Orthophosphate + Urea-1-carboxylate","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00002","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00002 + C00086 + C00288 <=> C00008 + C00009 + C01010","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00171","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"An adenine nucleotide containing three phosphate groups esterified to the sugar moiety. In addition to its crucial roles in metabolism adenosine triphosphate is a neurotransmitter. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"ATP + Urea + HCO3- <=> ADP + Orthophosphate + Urea-1-carboxylate","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00086","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00002 + C00086 + C00288 <=> C00008 + C00009 + C01010","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB03904","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"A compound formed in the liver from ammonia produced by the deamination of amino acids. It is the principal end product of protein catabolism and constitutes about one half of the total urinary solids. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
