{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Sulfur + Oxygen + H2O <=> Sulfite","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00051","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00087 + C00007 + C00001 <=> C00094","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00143","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"A tripeptide with many roles in cells.  It conjugates to drugs to make them more soluble for excretion, is a cofactor for some enzymes, is involved in protein disulfide bond rearrangement and reduces peroxides. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Nitric oxide + H2O + Ferricytochrome c <=> Nitrite + Ferrocytochrome c + H+","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00533","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00533 + C00001 + C00125 <=> C00088 + C00126 + C00080","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00435","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"Nitric oxide or Nitrogen monoxide is a chemical compound with chemical formula NO. This gas is an important signaling molecule in the body of mammals including humans and is an extremely important intermediate in the chemical industry. It is also a toxic air pollutant produced by automobile engines and power plants.\nNitric oxide (NO) should not be confused with nitrous oxide (N2O), a general anaesthetic, or with nitrogen dioxide (NO2) which is another poisonous air pollutant.\nThe nitric oxide molecule is a free radical, which is relevant to understanding its high reactivity. It reacts with the ozone in air to form nitrogen dioxide, signalled by the appearance of the reddish-brown color.","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Nitric oxide + H2O + Ferricytochrome c2 <=> Nitrite + Ferrocytochrome c2 + H+","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00533","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00533 + C00001 + C00997 <=> C00088 + C01000 + C00080","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00435","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"Nitric oxide or Nitrogen monoxide is a chemical compound with chemical formula NO. This gas is an important signaling molecule in the body of mammals including humans and is an extremely important intermediate in the chemical industry. It is also a toxic air pollutant produced by automobile engines and power plants.\nNitric oxide (NO) should not be confused with nitrous oxide (N2O), a general anaesthetic, or with nitrogen dioxide (NO2) which is another poisonous air pollutant.\nThe nitric oxide molecule is a free radical, which is relevant to understanding its high reactivity. It reacts with the ozone in air to form nitrogen dioxide, signalled by the appearance of the reddish-brown color.","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Nitric oxide + H2O + Oxidized azurin <=> Nitrite + Reduced azurin + 2 H+","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00533","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00533 + C00001 + C05357 <=> C00088 + C05358 + 2 C00080","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00435","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"Nitric oxide or Nitrogen monoxide is a chemical compound with chemical formula NO. This gas is an important signaling molecule in the body of mammals including humans and is an extremely important intermediate in the chemical industry. It is also a toxic air pollutant produced by automobile engines and power plants.\nNitric oxide (NO) should not be confused with nitrous oxide (N2O), a general anaesthetic, or with nitrogen dioxide (NO2) which is another poisonous air pollutant.\nThe nitric oxide molecule is a free radical, which is relevant to understanding its high reactivity. It reacts with the ozone in air to form nitrogen dioxide, signalled by the appearance of the reddish-brown color.","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Sucrose + Orthophosphate <=> D-Fructose + D-Glucose 1-phosphate","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00089","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00089 + C00009 <=> C00095 + C00103","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB02772","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"A nonreducing disaccharide composed of glucose and fructose linked via their anomeric carbons. It is obtained commercially from sugarcane, sugar beet (beta vulgaris), and other plants and used extensively as a food and a sweetener. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
