{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"sn-glycero-3-Phosphocholine + H2O <=> Choline + sn-Glycerol 3-phosphate","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00670","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00670 + C00001 <=> C00114 + C00093","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB04660","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"A component of phosphatidylcholines (lecithins), in which the two hydroxy groups of glycerol are esterified with fatty acids. (From Stedman, 26th ed) It counteracts the effects of urea on enzymes and other macromolecules. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"2-Chlorobenzoate + Oxygen + NADH + H+ <=> Chloride + Catechol + NAD+ + CO2","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00004","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C02357 + C00007 + C00004 + C00080 <=> C00115 + C00090 + C00003 +\tC00011","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00157","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"NADH is the reduced form of NAD+, and NAD+ is the oxidized form of NADH, A coenzyme composed of ribosylnicotinamide 5'-diphosphate coupled to adenosine 5'-phosphate by pyrophosphate linkage. It is found widely in nature and is involved in numerous enzymatic reactions in which it serves as an electron carrier by being alternately oxidized (NAD+) and reduced (NADH). It forms NADP with the addition of a phosphate group to the 2' position of the adenosyl nucleotide through an ester linkage.(Dorland, 27th ed)","type":"literal"}},
