{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"L-Histidine + S-Adenosyl-L-methionine <=> N(pi)-Methyl-L-histidine + S-Adenosyl-L-homocysteine","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00440","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00135 + C00019 <=> C01152 + C00021","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB04789","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"5-Methyltetrahydrofolate is a methylated derivate of tetrahydrofolate. It is generated by methylenetetrahydrofolate reductase from 5,10-methylenetetrahydrofolate and used to recycle homocysteine back to methionine by 5-methyltetrahydrofolate-homocysteine methyltransferases (also called methionine synthases).","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"L-Histidine + S-Adenosyl-L-methionine <=> N(pi)-Methyl-L-histidine + S-Adenosyl-L-homocysteine","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C08300","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00135 + C00019 <=> C01152 + C00021","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB01486","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"Cathine (��-hydroxyamphetamine) is a monoamine alkaloid found in the shrub Catha edulis (khat). Cathine is a Schedule III drug under the Convention on Psychotropic Substances. In the United States, it is classified as a Schedule IV controlled substance. [Wikipedia]","type":"literal"}},
