{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"3',5'-Cyclic GMP + H2O <=> GMP","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00942","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00942 + C00001 <=> C00144","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB02315","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"Guanosine cyclic 3&#39;,5&#39;-(hydrogen phosphate). A guanine nucleotide containing one phosphate group which is esterified to the sugar moiety in both the 3&#39;- and 5&#39;-positions. It is a cellular regulatory agent and has been described as a second messenger. Its levels increase in response to a variety of hormones, including acetylcholine, insulin, and oxytocin and it has been found to activate specific protein kinases. (From Merck Index, 11th ed)","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Thiol + S-Adenosyl-L-methionine <=> Sulfide + S-Adenosyl-L-homocysteine","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00019","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00145 + C00019 <=> C00297 + C00021","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00118","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"Physiologic methyl radical donor involved in enzymatic transmethylation reactions and present in all living organisms. It possesses anti-inflammatory activity and has been used in treatment of chronic liver disease. (From Merck, 11th ed)","type":"literal"}},
