{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"ATP + Ethanolamine <=> ADP + Ethanolamine phosphate","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00189","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00002 + C00189 <=> C00008 + C00346","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB03994","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"A viscous, hygroscopic amino alcohol with an ammoniacal odor. It is widely distributed in biological tissue and is a component of lecithin. It is used as a surfactant, fluorimetric reagent, and to remove CO2 and H2S from natural gas and other gases. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
