{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"(5Z,8Z,11Z,14Z)-Icosatetraenoic acid + 2 Oxygen <=> Prostaglandin G2","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00219","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00219 + 2 C00007 <=> C05956","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB04557","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"An unsaturated, essential fatty acid. It is found in animal and human fat as well as in the liver, brain, and glandular organs, and is a constituent of animal phosphatides. It is formed by the synthesis from dietary linoleic acid and is a precursor in the biosynthesis of prostaglandins, thromboxanes, and leukotrienes. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
