{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Succinate semialdehyde + Pyruvate <=> 2,4-Dihydroxyhept-2-enedioate","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00067","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00232 + C00022 <=> C06201","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB03843","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"A highly reactive aldehyde gas formed by oxidation or incomplete combustion of hydrocarbons. In solution, it has a wide range of uses: in the manufacture of resins and textiles, as a disinfectant, and as a laboratory fixative or preservative. Formaldehyde solution (formalin) is considered a hazardous compound, and its vapor toxic. (From Reynolds, Martindale The Extra Pharmacopoeia, 30th ed, p717)","type":"literal"}},
