{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Pyridoxamine + Pyruvate <=> Pyridoxal + L-Alanine","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00022","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00534 + C00022 <=> C00250 + C00041","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00119","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"An intermediate compound in the metabolism of carbohydrates, proteins, and fats. In thiamine deficiency, its oxidation is retarded and it accumulates in the tissues, especially in nervous structures. (From Stedman, 26th ed)","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Chorismate + L-Glutamine <=> 4-Amino-4-deoxychorismate + L-Glutamate","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00064","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00251 + C00064 <=> C11355 + C00025","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00130","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"A non-essential amino acid present abundantly throughout the body and is involved in many metabolic processes. It is synthesized from glutamic acid and ammonia. It is the principal carrier of nitrogen in the body and is an important energy source for many cells. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Nicotinate + NADP+ + H2O <=> 6-Hydroxynicotinate + NADPH + H+","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00253","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00253 + C00006 + C00001 <=> C01020 + C00005 + C00080","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00627","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"A water-soluble vitamin of the B complex occurring in various animal and plant tissues. It is required by the body for the formation of coenzymes NAD and NADP. It has pellagra-curative, vasodilating, and antilipemic properties. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
