{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Tetrahydrobiopterin + L-Phenylalanine + Oxygen <=> Dihydrobiopterin + L-Tyrosine + H2O","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00079","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00272 + C00079 + C00007 <=> C00268 + C00082 + C00001","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00120","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"An essential aromatic amino acid that is a precursor of melanin; dopamine; noradrenalin (norepinephrine), and thyroxine. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Tetrahydrobiopterin + L-Phenylalanine + Oxygen <=> Dihydrobiopterin + L-Tyrosine + H2O","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00272","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00272 + C00079 + C00007 <=> C00268 + C00082 + C00001","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00360","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"Tetrahydrobiopterin or BH4 is a cofactor in the synthesis of nitric oxide. It is also essential in the conversion of phenylalanine to tyrosine by the enzyme phenylalanine-4-hydroxylase; the conversion of tyrosine to L-dopa by the enzyme tyrosine hydroxylase; and conversion of tryptophan to 5-hydroxytryptophan via tryptophan hydroxylase. [Wikipedia]","type":"literal"}},
