{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Tetrahydrobiopterin + L-Tryptophan + Oxygen <=> 5-Hydroxy-L-tryptophan + Dihydrobiopterin + H2O","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00078","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00272 + C00078 + C00007 <=> C00643 + C00268 + C00001","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00150","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"An essential amino acid that is necessary for normal growth in infants and for nitrogen balance in adults. It is a precursor of indole alkaloids in plants. It is a precursor of serotonin (hence its use as an antidepressant and sleep aid). It can be a precursor to niacin, albeit inefficiently, in mammals. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
