{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Sucrose + Amylose <=> D-Fructose + Amylose","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00089","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00089 + C00718 <=> C00095 + C00718","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB02772","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"A nonreducing disaccharide composed of glucose and fructose linked via their anomeric carbons. It is obtained commercially from sugarcane, sugar beet (beta vulgaris), and other plants and used extensively as a food and a sweetener. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Androst-4-ene-3,17-dione + Reduced acceptor + Oxygen <=> Testololactone + Acceptor + H2O","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00280","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00280 + C00030 + C00007 <=> C04676 + C00028 + C00001","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB01536","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"A delta-4 C19 steroid that is produced not only in the testis, but also in the ovary and the adrenal cortex.  Depending on the tissue type, androstenedione can serve as a precursor to testosterone as well as estrone and estradiol. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Testosterone + NAD+ <=> Androst-4-ene-3,17-dione + NADH + H+","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00535","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00535 + C00003 <=> C00280 + C00004 + C00080","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00624","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"A potent androgenic steroid and major product secreted by the leydig cells of the testis. Its production is stimulated by luteinizing hormone from the pituitary gland. In turn, testosterone exerts feedback control of the pituitary LH and FSH secretion. Depending on the tissues, testosterone can be further converted to dihydrotestosterone or estradiol. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
