{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Inosine + Orthophosphate <=> Hypoxanthine + alpha-D-Ribose 1-phosphate","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00387","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00294 + C00009 <=> C00262 + C00620","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB02857","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"Guanosine is a nucleoside comprising guanine attached to a ribose (ribofuranose) ring via a ��-N9-glycosidic bond. Guanosine can be phosphorylated to become GMP (guanosine monophosphate), cGMP (cyclic guanosine monophosphate), GDP (guanosine diphosphate) and GTP (guanosine triphosphate). [Wikipedia]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Quinate + PQQ <=> PQQH2 + 3-Dehydroquinate","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00113","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00296 + C00113 <=> C01359 + C00944","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB03205","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"A pyrrolo-quinoline having two adjacent keto-groups at the 4 and 5 positions and three acidic carboxyl groups. It is a coenzyme of some DEHYDROGENASES. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"D-Cysteine + H2O <=> Hydrogen sulfide + NH3 + Pyruvate","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00793","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00793 + C00001 <=> C00283 + C00014 + C00022","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB03201","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"A thiol-containing non-essential amino acid that is oxidized to form CYSTINE. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Thiosulfate + 2 Glutathione + H+ <=> Sulfite + Glutathione disulfide + Hydrogen sulfide","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00051","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00320 + 2 C00051 + C00080 <=> C00094 + C00127 + C00283","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00143","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"A tripeptide with many roles in cells.  It conjugates to drugs to make them more soluble for excretion, is a cofactor for some enzymes, is involved in protein disulfide bond rearrangement and reduces peroxides. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Deoxyuridine + 2-Oxoglutarate + Oxygen <=> Uridine + Succinate + CO2","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00526","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00526 + C00026 + C00007 <=> C00299 + C00042 + C00011","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB02256","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"2&#39;-Deoxyuridine. An antimetabolite that is converted to deoxyuridine triphosphate during DNA synthesis. Laboratory suppression of deoxyuridine is used to diagnose megaloblastic anemias due to vitamin B12 and folate deficiencies. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
