{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"ATP + Pyridoxine <=> ADP + Pyridoxine phosphate","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00250","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00002 + C00314 <=> C00008 + C00627","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00147","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"The 4-carboxyaldehyde form of vitamin B 6 which is converted to pyridoxal phosphate which is a coenzyme for synthesis of amino acids, neurotransmitters (serotonin, norepinephrine), sphingolipids, aminolevulinic acid. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Pyridoxine + Oxygen <=> Isopyridoxal + H2O2","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00314","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00314 + C00007 <=> C06051 + C00027","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00165","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"The 4-methanol form of vitamin B 6 which is converted to pyridoxal phosphate which is a coenzyme for synthesis of amino acids, neurotransmitters (serotonin, norepinephrine), sphingolipids, aminolevulinic acid.  Although pyridoxine and Vitamin B 6 are still frequently used as synonyms, especially by medical researchers, this practice is erroneous and sometimes misleading (EE Snell; Ann NY Acad Sci, vol 585 pg 1, 1990). [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Pyridoxine + Orthophosphate <=> Pyridoxine phosphate + H2O","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00018","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00314 + C00009 <=> C00627 + C00001","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00114","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"This is the active form of vitamin B 6 serving as a coenzyme for synthesis of amino acids, neurotransmitters (serotonin, norepinephrine), sphingolipids, aminolevulinic acid.  During transamination of amino acids, pyridoxal phosphate is transiently converted into pyridoxamine phosphate (pyridoxamine). [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"UDP-glucose + Pyridoxine <=> UDP + 5'-O-beta-D-Glucosylpyridoxine","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00314","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00029 + C00314 <=> C00015 + C03996","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00165","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"The 4-methanol form of vitamin B 6 which is converted to pyridoxal phosphate which is a coenzyme for synthesis of amino acids, neurotransmitters (serotonin, norepinephrine), sphingolipids, aminolevulinic acid.  Although pyridoxine and Vitamin B 6 are still frequently used as synonyms, especially by medical researchers, this practice is erroneous and sometimes misleading (EE Snell; Ann NY Acad Sci, vol 585 pg 1, 1990). [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Spermidine + Oxygen + H2O <=> 1,3-Diaminopropane + 4-Aminobutanal + H2O2","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00315","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00315 + C00007 + C00001 <=> C00986 + C00555 + C00027","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB03566","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"Spermidine is a polyamine formed from putrescine. It is found in almost all tissues in association with nucleic acids. It is found as a cation at all pH values, and is thought to help stabilize some membranes and nucleic acid structures. It is a precursor of spermine.","type":"literal"}},
