{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"ATP + L-Citrulline + L-Aspartate <=> AMP + Diphosphate + N-(L-Arginino)succinate","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00327","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00002 + C00327 + C00049 <=> C00020 + C00013 + C03406","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00155","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"Citrulline is an amino acid.  It is made from ornithine and carbamoyl phosphate in one of the central reactions in the urea cycle. It is also produced from arginine as a by-product of the reaction catalyzed by NOS family.  Its name is derived from citrullus, the Latin word for watermelon, from which it was first isolated.","type":"literal"}},
