{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Deoxyguanosine + Orthophosphate <=> Guanine + 2-Deoxy-D-ribose 1-phosphate","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00214","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00330 + C00009 <=> C00242 + C00672","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB04485","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"Deoxythymidine is a pyrimidine deoxynucleoside. Deoxythymidine is the DNA nucleoside T, which pairs with deoxyadenosine (A) in double-stranded DNA. In cell biology it is used to synchronize the cells in S phase.","type":"literal"}},
