{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"(-)-Menthol + NADP+ <=> (-)-Menthone + NADPH + H+","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00400","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00400 + C00006 <=> C00843 + C00005 + C00080","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00825","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"Menthol is a covalent organic compound made synthetically or obtained from peppermint or other mint oils. It is a waxy, crystalline substance, clear or white in color, which is solid at room temperature and melts slightly above. The main form of menthol occurring in nature is (-)-menthol, which is assigned the (1R,2S,5R) configuration. Menthol has local anesthetic and counterirritant qualities, and it is widely used to relieve minor throat irritation.","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"(-)-Menthol + Oxygen + NADPH + H+ <=> p-Menthane-3,8-diol + NADP+ + H2O","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00400","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00400 + C00007 + C00005 + C00080 <=> C02904 + C00006 + C00001","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00825","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"Menthol is a covalent organic compound made synthetically or obtained from peppermint or other mint oils. It is a waxy, crystalline substance, clear or white in color, which is solid at room temperature and melts slightly above. The main form of menthol occurring in nature is (-)-menthol, which is assigned the (1R,2S,5R) configuration. Menthol has local anesthetic and counterirritant qualities, and it is widely used to relieve minor throat irritation.","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"UDP-glucose + (-)-Menthol <=> UDP + (-)-Menthyl O-beta-D-glucoside","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00400","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00029 + C00400 <=> C00015 + C03962","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00825","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"Menthol is a covalent organic compound made synthetically or obtained from peppermint or other mint oils. It is a waxy, crystalline substance, clear or white in color, which is solid at room temperature and melts slightly above. The main form of menthol occurring in nature is (-)-menthol, which is assigned the (1R,2S,5R) configuration. Menthol has local anesthetic and counterirritant qualities, and it is widely used to relieve minor throat irritation.","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"ATP + (Phosphate)n <=> ADP + (Phosphate)n","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00002","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00002 + C00404 <=> C00008 + C00404","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00171","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"An adenine nucleotide containing three phosphate groups esterified to the sugar moiety. In addition to its crucial roles in metabolism adenosine triphosphate is a neurotransmitter. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
