{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"L-Valine + (S)-3-Methyl-2-oxopentanoic acid <=> 3-Methyl-2-oxobutanoic acid + L-Isoleucine","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00183","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00183 + C00671 <=> C00141 + C00407","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00161","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"A branched-chain essential amino acid that has stimulant activity. It promotes muscle growth and tissue repair. It is a precursor in the penicillin biosynthetic pathway. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"L-Pipecolate + NAD+ <=> delta1-Piperideine-2-carboxylate + NADH + H+","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00148","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00408 + C00003 <=> C04092 + C00004 + C00080","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00172","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"A non-essential amino acid that is synthesized from glutamic acid. It is an essential component of collagen and is important for proper functioning of joints and tendons. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"L-Pipecolate + NADP+ <=> delta1-Piperideine-2-carboxylate + NADPH + H+","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00148","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00408 + C00006 <=> C04092 + C00005 + C00080","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00172","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"A non-essential amino acid that is synthesized from glutamic acid. It is an essential component of collagen and is important for proper functioning of joints and tendons. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Progesterone + Oxygen + NADPH + H+ <=> Testosterone acetate + NADP+ + H2O","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00280","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00410 + C00007 + C00005 + C00080 <=> C03027 + C00006 + C00001","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB01536","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"A delta-4 C19 steroid that is produced not only in the testis, but also in the ovary and the adrenal cortex.  Depending on the tissue type, androstenedione can serve as a precursor to testosterone as well as estrone and estradiol. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Progesterone + Oxygen + NADPH + H+ <=> Testosterone acetate + NADP+ + H2O","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00410","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00410 + C00007 + C00005 + C00080 <=> C03027 + C00006 + C00001","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00396","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"The major progestational steroid that is secreted primarily by the corpus luteum and the placenta. Progesterone acts on the uterus, the mammary glands and the brain. It is required in embryo implantation; pregnancy maintenance, and the development of mammary tissue for milk production. Progesterone, converted from pregnenolone, also serves as an intermediate in the biosynthesis of gonadal steroid hormones and adrenal corticosteroids. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Progesterone + Reduced acceptor + Oxygen <=> Testosterone acetate + Acceptor + H2O","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00410","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00410 + C00030 + C00007 <=> C03027 + C00028 + C00001","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00396","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"The major progestational steroid that is secreted primarily by the corpus luteum and the placenta. Progesterone acts on the uterus, the mammary glands and the brain. It is required in embryo implantation; pregnancy maintenance, and the development of mammary tissue for milk production. Progesterone, converted from pregnenolone, also serves as an intermediate in the biosynthesis of gonadal steroid hormones and adrenal corticosteroids. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Progesterone + Reduced acceptor + Oxygen <=> 11alpha-Hydroxyprogesterone + Acceptor + H2O","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00410","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00410 + C00030 + C00007 <=> C03747 + C00028 + C00001","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00396","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"The major progestational steroid that is secreted primarily by the corpus luteum and the placenta. Progesterone acts on the uterus, the mammary glands and the brain. It is required in embryo implantation; pregnancy maintenance, and the development of mammary tissue for milk production. Progesterone, converted from pregnenolone, also serves as an intermediate in the biosynthesis of gonadal steroid hormones and adrenal corticosteroids. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"ATP + Sinapate + CoA <=> AMP + Diphosphate + Sinapoyl-CoA","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00002","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00002 + C00482 + C00010 <=> C00020 + C00013 + C00411","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00171","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"An adenine nucleotide containing three phosphate groups esterified to the sugar moiety. In addition to its crucial roles in metabolism adenosine triphosphate is a neurotransmitter. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Stearoyl-CoA + Malonyl-CoA + 2 NADH + 2 H+ <=> Eicosanoyl-CoA + CO2 + 2 NAD+ + CoA + H2O","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00004","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00412 + C00083 + 2 C00004 + 2 C00080 <=> C02041 + C00011 + 2 C00003\t+ C00010 + C00001","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00157","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"NADH is the reduced form of NAD+, and NAD+ is the oxidized form of NADH, A coenzyme composed of ribosylnicotinamide 5'-diphosphate coupled to adenosine 5'-phosphate by pyrophosphate linkage. It is found widely in nature and is involved in numerous enzymatic reactions in which it serves as an electron carrier by being alternately oxidized (NAD+) and reduced (NADH). It forms NADP with the addition of a phosphate group to the 2' position of the adenosyl nucleotide through an ester linkage.(Dorland, 27th ed)","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Stearoyl-CoA + Malonyl-CoA + 2 NADH + 2 H+ <=> Eicosanoyl-CoA + CO2 + 2 NAD+ + CoA + H2O","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00083","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00412 + C00083 + 2 C00004 + 2 C00080 <=> C02041 + C00011 + 2 C00003\t+ C00010 + C00001","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB04524","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"A coenzyme A derivative which plays a key role in the fatty acid synthesis in the cytoplasmic and microsomal systems. [PubChem]","type":"literal"}},
{"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Stearoyl-CoA + Malonyl-CoA + 2 NADPH + 2 H+ <=> Eicosanoyl-CoA + CO2 + 2 NADP+ + CoA + H2O","type":"literal"},"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00004","type":"uri"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00412 + C00083 + 2 C00005 + 2 C00080 <=> C02041 + C00011 + 2 C00006\t+ C00010 + C00001","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00157","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"NADH is the reduced form of NAD+, and NAD+ is the oxidized form of NADH, A coenzyme composed of ribosylnicotinamide 5'-diphosphate coupled to adenosine 5'-phosphate by pyrophosphate linkage. It is found widely in nature and is involved in numerous enzymatic reactions in which it serves as an electron carrier by being alternately oxidized (NAD+) and reduced (NADH). It forms NADP with the addition of a phosphate group to the 2' position of the adenosyl nucleotide through an ester linkage.(Dorland, 27th ed)","type":"literal"}}
